
<div class="container mt-5 mb-5">

  <h1 class="text-center mb-4">About BookNest 📚</h1>

  <p class="lead text-center mb-5">
    BookNest is a Ruby on Rails web application that
    allows users to explore a collection of books,
    authors, and categories.
  </p>

  <div class="card shadow-sm mb-4">
    <div class="card-body">
      <h2>Project Overview</h2>
      <p>
        The purpose of BookNest is to demonstrate
        database relationships, data collection,
        navigation, and information retrieval using
        Ruby on Rails and ActiveRecord.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>

<!-- Data Sources -->
<div class="card shadow-sm mb-4">
  <div class="card-body">
    <h2>Data Sources</h2>

    <p>
      BookNest uses Faker to generate sample book titles,
      author information, descriptions, and prices.
    </p>

    <p>
      Five classic books were also manually added using
      real bibliographic information, including titles,
      authors, and publication years.
      Open Library is listed as a bibliographic reference.
    </p>

    <p>
      Ten predefined book categories are included.
    </p>

    <ul>
      <li>255 Books</li>
      <li>25 Authors</li>
      <li>10 Categories</li>
      <li>290 Total Records</li>
    </ul>

    <p>
      <strong>References:</strong>
      <a href="https://github.com/faker-ruby/faker"
         target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Faker</a>
      |
      <a href="https://openlibrary.org/"
         target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Open Library</a>
    </p>
  </div>
</div>


  <div class="card shadow-sm mb-4">
    <div class="card-body">
      <h2>Database Structure</h2>

      <h3>Authors Table</h3>
      <p>
        Stores author names, countries, and biographies.
      </p>

      <h3>Categories Table</h3>
      <p>
        Stores book categories and their descriptions.
      </p>

      <h3>Books Table</h3>
      <p>
        Stores book titles, descriptions, prices,
        publication years, and references to authors
        and categories.
      </p>

      <h3>Database Relationships</h3>
      <ul>
        <li>One author can have many books.</li>
        <li>One category can have many books.</li>
        <li>Each book belongs to one author.</li>
        <li>Each book belongs to one category.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="card shadow-sm mb-4">
    <div class="card-body">
      <h2>Technologies Used</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Ruby on Rails</li>
        <li>SQLite Database</li>
        <li>ActiveRecord ORM</li>
        <li>Faker Gem</li>
        <li>Bootstrap 5</li>
        <li>Kaminari (Pagination)</li>
        <li>HTML and ERB</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </div>

</div>
